flowchart TB

MEA["`MEASURED — 28 runs versioned in the repo
single core · one IP per request so the
rate limiter does not cap the test
AI paths excluded to keep model latency
out of CRUD latency`"]

TAB["`250 users → 33 req/s · p95 26 ms · 0% fail
500 users → 65 req/s · p95 46 ms · 0% fail
750 users → 99 req/s · p95 545 ms · 0% fail
— recommended ceiling on this machine
1,000 users → 120 req/s · p95 1.1 s · 0.2%
1,500 users → 89% fail
1 → 4 workers: 66 → 140 req/s, same code`"]

END["`ENDURANCE
112,549 requests in 9 min · 208 req/s
· 0% fail · p95 75 ms
long run: 1.26M requests in 3 h 34 min
· 300 users · 0.26% fail
total measured: 2.45M requests`"]

CALC["`CALCULATED — arithmetic, not measurement
0.13 req/s per user (99 ÷ 750)
80k users ≈ 10,600 req/s
1M users ≈ 130,000 req/s
180 req/s per worker as a conservative
per-core capacity · +40% headroom for
peaks, deploys and losing a zone`"]

LB["`CLOUD LOAD BALANCER — production
in front of the Traefiks,
spreads traffic across zones`"]

TRAEFIK["`TRAEFIK — distributes requests
across API replicas · discovers containers
by Docker labels · API is STATELESS:
no sticky sessions, any replica serves
any user — horizontal scale stays simple
gap: LB health check not configured yet;
a readiness endpoint (checks PostgreSQL
and Redis) already exists — first fix
before running multiple replicas`"]

UVI["`UVICORN
more workers per container`"]

PGB["`PGBOUNCER
controls the PostgreSQL
connection pool`"]

CEL["`CELERY
spreads background work
across machines`"]

BOT["`EXPECTED BOTTLENECKS — shared resources,
in order: PostgreSQL connection count
→ read capacity (replicas + Redis cache)
→ Redis contention
→ Argon2 CPU during login peaks
conclusion: the architecture reaches 1M users,
but not by only adding containers — database,
cache, workers and auth infra grow with it`"]

MEA --> TAB
MEA --> END
TAB --> CALC
CALC --> LB
LB --> TRAEFIK --> UVI --> PGB
TRAEFIK -.- CEL
PGB --> BOT

